{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The set of all real solutions of the inequality \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/9/4c9eeee7dbb1d7cce72993f8882748c32d90ec5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|x - 1| + |x + 2| &lt; 5\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e86913db5611e86878aa4e1ee2deec55db56423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ x \\in ( - 3,2) \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ x \\in ( - 1,2) \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ x \\in ( - 2,1) \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"429\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e6587e0a83074ae4f12d4a531eec9b00acc22a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ x \\in \\left( - \\frac32,\\frac72\\right) \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\O \\text{ (empty})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"288\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can do casework upon the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. First, consider the case where both absolute values are positive, which is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791aa0ff911a09ac656cd5ce7638ca8e64805d8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />. In this case, the equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac1d93f5172acdfa0efd2e394a718fcee45b0c66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 1 &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />. This turns into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84958f805b063032d2629160e880abc1487afa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Combining this with our original assumption, we get the solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/4880bb89c7a100539a9ede3ef33be466c2817782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq x &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Next, consider the case when both absolute values are negative, which is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad0c22ee68fa46b5dd4e00d5483346ca9b7ccc28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />. This yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c172494e478b06cf59979cfeababe0df04c36737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 - 2x &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"97\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae6d42763ba7b01b63ffd829e70b066f2e6f1c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. Combining this with our original assumption, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f121b19a2f5dbe5f9634ff08b428c275f7839286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3 &lt; x &lt; -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>The next case is when the first absolute value is positive and the second is negative. This occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791aa0ff911a09ac656cd5ce7638ca8e64805d8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad0c22ee68fa46b5dd4e00d5483346ca9b7ccc28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />. Obviously, this has no solutions, since the inequalities do not overlap.\n</p><p>The final case is when the first absolute value is negative and the second is positive. This occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1faf5d41cd05857f8f0cbab1eb5a41bb1a6741f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76cbe818acc48517195703ff7f38cfb5b39e2e35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />. This yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/5/7150342c81553bfa3a9ab39b2669fb2af17e6345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, which is always true. Therefore, we also get the solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f3321b7c0b2052388ebb0be8b518f856636638e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2 \\leq x &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, after combining all of our solutions, we get the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89227035a5d6e3a8f97c74b9f08dd3ba52f1d93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3 &lt; x &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc308ff37f94838c11808d9746f10ba1ac15deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1973 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"19